{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967966-game-management-tools","id":967966,"title":"Game Management Tools","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-12T09:06:36-07:00","id":967966,"title":"Game Management Tools","content":"So I'm starting to do the planning for a Hunter game set in 80s Miami, a sort of goofy hodge-podge of pop culture modeled in terms of game play on video games like Grand Theft Auto: Vice City (open world with a group of incompetent criminals trying to pay off a mob boss and rise to fame and fortune). As such, I'm going to have a whole lot of material to organize, and this is going to be the first game I've run in a very long time.<br /> <br /> So what kind of tools does everyone use to manage their games? I figured I'd use Evernote as my alternative to stacks of notebooks, but I was wondering if there are any useful (preferably free) products people know of that can help streamline the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:10:39-07:00","id":967968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967966-game-management-tools#post967966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm starting to do the planning for a Hunter game set in 80s Miami, a sort of goofy hodge-podge of pop culture modeled in terms of game play on video games like Grand Theft Auto: Vice City (open world with a group of incompetent criminals trying to pay off a mob boss and rise to fame and fortune). As such, I'm going to have a whole lot of material to organize, and this is going to be the first game I've run in a very long time.<br /> <br /> So what kind of tools does everyone use to manage their games? I figured I'd use Evernote as my alternative to stacks of notebooks, but I was wondering if there are any useful (preferably free) products people know of that can help streamline the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm from Miami! Let me know if me (or my parents) can answer any Miami questions for you.<br /> <br /> I use ObsidianPortal. There's a wiki section where you can post info for your setting, a section for character sheets, you can keep GM secrets, there's an Adventure Log, you can put up a map, and a lot more. Would it be helpful if I posted one of my campaign pages for you to see?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:11:26-07:00","id":967970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967966-game-management-tools#post967966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm starting to do the planning for a Hunter game set in 80s Miami, a sort of goofy hodge-podge of pop culture modeled in terms of game play on video games like Grand Theft Auto: Vice City (open world with a group of incompetent criminals trying to pay off a mob boss and rise to fame and fortune). As such, I'm going to have a whole lot of material to organize, and this is going to be the first game I've run in a very long time.<br /> <br /> So what kind of tools does everyone use to manage their games? I figured I'd use Evernote as my alternative to stacks of notebooks, but I was wondering if there are any useful (preferably free) products people know of that can help streamline the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just make a parent folder for the Chronicle in my Google Drive, then make subfolders for each Story. In the Story folders, I have folders for NPCs, Locations, and PC Notes (and often I share the PC folder with my players). In the Story folders I also put docs with my private notes and musings and would put stuff like flowcharts there if I ever bothered to scan them. PC Notes is usually the largest folder because it'll also have stuff like the Ladder in Vampire: The Requiem, and allied NPCs that the players can look at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:15:09-07:00","id":967972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967966-game-management-tools?p=967968#post967968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm from Miami! Let me know if me (or my parents) can answer any Miami questions for you.<br /> <br /> I use ObsidianPortal. There's a wiki section where you can post info for your setting, a section for character sheets, you can keep GM secrets, there's an Adventure Log, you can put up a map, and a lot more. Would it be helpful if I posted one of my campaign pages for you to see?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be great actually. I'm going for a fictionalized version of the city, sort of the larger-than-life TV version of Miami in the 80s, but the one thing I'm having trouble finding is the breakdown of the neighborhoods. I'd like to have something that at least resembles the layout of the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:16:51-07:00","id":967974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967966-game-management-tools?p=967970#post967970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just make a parent folder for the Chronicle in my Google Drive, then make subfolders for each Story. In the Story folders, I have folders for NPCs, Locations, and PC Notes (and often I share the PC folder with my players). In the Story folders I also put docs with my private notes and musings and would put stuff like flowcharts there if I ever bothered to scan them. PC Notes is usually the largest folder because it'll also have stuff like the Ladder in Vampire: The Requiem, and allied NPCs that the players can look at.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I might try something similar. I'm going for more of an open ended approach. It's basically going to be &quot;You got hired for this job. Shit went south, your employer got murdered and now you owe a quarter million dollars to a vicious monster&quot;, and then throw the players into a sandbox and let them go to town however they feel like, so I probably won't split things up into stories, but I could easily do something similar with separate folders for different territories and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:21:17-07:00","id":967977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967966-game-management-tools?p=967974#post967974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I might try something similar. I'm going for more of an open ended approach. It's basically going to be &quot;You got hired for this job. Shit went south, your employer got murdered and now you owe a quarter million dollars to a vicious monster&quot;, and then throw the players into a sandbox and let them go to town however they feel like, so I probably won't split things up into stories, but I could easily do something similar with separate folders for different territories and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be another good way to do it. Rather than break things up by territory, I might have NPCs and Territories folders which each reference each other a bunch: NPC subfolders would have documents detailing which territories they're invested in, and Territory subfolders would have docs with which NPCs are established there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:25:34-07:00","id":967981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967966-game-management-tools?p=967972#post967972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That would be great actually. I'm going for a fictionalized version of the city, sort of the larger-than-life TV version of Miami in the 80s, but the one thing I'm having trouble finding is the breakdown of the neighborhoods. I'd like to have something that at least resembles the layout of the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the ObsidianPortal page I used for a game set in Montreal in a rebellion trying to overthrow a dystopian North American government in the 2080s. You'll be able to see what tools you'll have at your disposal on the platform.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://torren-s-north-america.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://torren-s-north-america.obsidianportal.com/</a><br /> <br /> Depending on whether or not the game you're running will be in-person, I've found it super helpful to buy laminated maps from Barnes and Noble, and then I'll use dry-erase markers on them to show the group where they are, where things are going on (in the game above, which parts of the city were controlled by the government and which parts were controlled by the rebellion), etc. I know you might not be using the real map, but if you decide you do want to, I found this one you can buy. It's updated for 2015, so maybe not exactly what you're looking for, but you can probably find 80s maps if you look. I'll leave that one to you:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/streetwise-miami-map-laminated-city-center-street-map-of-miami-florida-folding-pocket-size-travel-map-with-metro-streetwise-maps/1117061069\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://prodimage.images-bn.com/pimages/9780935039511_p0_v2_s1200x630.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/streetwise-miami-map-laminated-city-center-street-map-of-miami-florida-folding-pocket-size-travel-map-with-metro-streetwise-maps/1117061069\" target=\"_blank\"> Streetwise Miami Map - Laminated City Center Street Map of Miami, Florida - Folding Pocket Size Travel Map With Metro (2013)|Other Format </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/streetwise-miami-map-laminated-city-center-street-map-of-miami-florida-folding-pocket-size-travel-map-with-metro-streetwise-maps/1117061069\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/streetwise-miami-map-laminated-city-center-street-map-of-miami-florida-folding-pocket-size-travel-map-with-metro-streetwise-maps/1117061069 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> 2013 UPDATED Streetwise Miami Map - Laminated City Center Street Map of Miami, Florida - Folding pocket size travel map with integrated metrorail &amp; metromover lines &amp; stationsThis map covers the following areas&amp;#58;Main Miami Map 1&amp;#58;24,000North Miami Beach Map 1&amp;#58;33,000&lt;BR... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Please let me know how I can help with stories of growing up in Miami. My mom grew up in Miami. My dad (born in 1957) moved down from New Jersey, but he's a lawyer and was involved in drug law when he first started up. John Gotti asked him to be his attorney but he turned him down, side-story. Obviously, that's New York, but a lot of organized crime is connected. And my dad's work on drug law was in FL.<br /> <br /> My mom is just a little younger, but she has stories about schooling, what kids growing up in Miami learned in school (which might be useful for you to set the tone and timber, as well as situate any PCs who were born in Miami). Let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T09:38:24-07:00","id":967985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967966-game-management-tools?p=967977#post967977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That'd be another good way to do it. Rather than break things up by territory, I might have NPCs and Territories folders which each reference each other a bunch: NPC subfolders would have documents detailing which territories they're invested in, and Territory subfolders would have docs with which NPCs are established there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I can do something similar with Evernote, with cross references and a sort of Table of Contents, but I'm just going to have to mess around with it and see what it's capable of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967966-game-management-tools?p=967981#post967981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the ObsidianPortal page I used for a game set in Montreal in a rebellion trying to overthrow a dystopian North American government in the 2080s. You'll be able to see what tools you'll have at your disposal on the platform.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://torren-s-north-america.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://torren-s-north-america.obsidianportal.com/</a><br /> <br /> Depending on whether or not the game you're running will be in-person, I've found it super helpful to buy laminated maps from Barnes and Noble, and then I'll use dry-erase markers on them to show the group where they are, where things are going on (in the game above, which parts of the city were controlled by the government and which parts were controlled by the rebellion), etc. I know you might not be using the real map, but if you decide you do want to, I found this one you can buy. It's updated for 2015, so maybe not exactly what you're looking for, but you can probably find 80s maps if you look. I'll leave that one to you:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/streetwise-miami-map-laminated-city-center-street-map-of-miami-florida-folding-pocket-size-travel-map-with-metro-streetwise-maps/1117061069\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://prodimage.images-bn.com/pimages/9780935039511_p0_v2_s1200x630.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/streetwise-miami-map-laminated-city-center-street-map-of-miami-florida-folding-pocket-size-travel-map-with-metro-streetwise-maps/1117061069\" target=\"_blank\"> Streetwise Miami Map - Laminated City Center Street Map of Miami, Florida - Folding Pocket Size Travel Map With Metro (2013)|Other Format </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/streetwise-miami-map-laminated-city-center-street-map-of-miami-florida-folding-pocket-size-travel-map-with-metro-streetwise-maps/1117061069\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/streetwise-miami-map-laminated-city-center-street-map-of-miami-florida-folding-pocket-size-travel-map-with-metro-streetwise-maps/1117061069 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> 2013 UPDATED Streetwise Miami Map - Laminated City Center Street Map of Miami, Florida - Folding pocket size travel map with integrated metrorail &amp; metromover lines &amp; stationsThis map covers the following areas&amp;#58;Main Miami Map 1&amp;#58;24,000North Miami Beach Map 1&amp;#58;33,000&lt;BR... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Please let me know how I can help with stories of growing up in Miami. My mom grew up in Miami. My dad (born in 1957) moved down from New Jersey, but he's a lawyer and was involved in drug law when he first started up. John Gotti asked him to be his attorney but he turned him down, side-story. Obviously, that's New York, but a lot of organized crime is connected. And my dad's work on drug law was in FL.<br /> <br /> My mom is just a little younger, but she has stories about schooling, what kids growing up in Miami learned in school (which might be useful for you to set the tone and timber, as well as situate any PCs who were born in Miami). Let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great! I'll definitely check out your page once I'm done with today's work. and the laminated map is a GREAT idea. It's going to be a face-to-face game, and I'll probably be using my tablet/laptop as a sort of interactive game tool, but having a big physical map with territories sketched out would really help with immersion I think.<br /> <br /> I'll probably hit you up for advice once I start sketching out the gangs and territories. It's going to be more of a cartoon version of Miami, but being able to root things in real experience could be incredibly useful. Can I just drop you a PM if I need anything? Also, yes, I was definitely planning on having the New York families play a part in the game -- I'm picturing about 1983, as refugees are pouring into the city, with Cuban smugglers and drug lords dominating the crime scene and the New York families trying to muscle their way in and carve off their slice of the pie.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Does anyone know of a good, free dice roller for CoD? Preferably one that can run on phones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T10:16:56-07:00","id":968007,"title":"","content":"My group uses one note","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T12:41:07-07:00","id":968081,"title":"","content":"I also use ObsidianPortal.<br /> <br /> Her's some links to my games as well:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://to-rule-in-hell.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://to-rule-in-hell.obsidianportal.com/</a> (Short lived Demon Game)<br /> <a href=\"https://the-valley-of-the-shadow-of-death.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://the-valley-of-the-shadow-of-...ianportal.com/</a> (Upcoming Crossover Game)<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing that you can't see when just browsing is that every page has multiple sections one of which only the GM can see the others the players can see as well. It's good for putting notes that the players don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T02:54:25-07:00","id":969112,"title":"","content":"Dropbox with a lot... A LOT text files and graphics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also I store in subfolders char sheets of NPCs.<br /> <br /> My players get one folder on each group where there are char sheets and info they want share with co-players. Sometimes I use Google Docs for making one-on-one sessions/scenes by net, as it nicely can be edited and easily explored in to cohesive plot write up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:33:09-07:00","id":970334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967966-game-management-tools?p=967968#post967968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm from Miami! Let me know if me (or my parents) can answer any Miami questions for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever witnessed personally an instance of &quot;Florida Man&quot; happenstance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:36:35-07:00","id":970335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/967966-game-management-tools?p=970334#post970334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you ever witnessed personally an instance of &quot;Florida Man&quot; happenstance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like personally seen one? Um. Nothing comes to mind. Like that I saw myself? I went to undergrad outside Florida when I was seventeen and I never drove, so I guess I wasn't all that exposed to that kind of thing =P. But I know of things and people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:58:36-07:00","id":973498,"title":"","content":"Some friends of mine use Trello to manage the status of plot/subplot points, etc, and usually attach things like NPC pictures and maps to the different cards. Apparently it has really helped keep relevant information close at hand, and gives a nice big picture view of what is happening (and what's been untouched for some time, if you use the card decay power-up).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cThe good sleep better, but the bad seem to enjoy the waking hours much more.\u201d</b> -<i>Woody Allen</i> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5322-zimthehacker","name":"Zimthehacker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5322_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:51:42-07:00","id":976544,"title":"","content":"We had our first session last week, and I think it went really well. I didn't end up using Obsidian Portal, because I'm not expecting my characters to keep up with a wiki, and so far Evernote has been working really well for what I need. I have characters (including sheets), sites, neighborhoods, and organizations in easily accessible folders, and my computer flips into a tablet, so I can easily share relevant information with the characters (Their first job is a heist, and their lawyer character pulled up a blueprint for the mansion). I also set up a mechanics folder with cheat sheets for things like conditions, standard rolls, and weapon parameters. It's my first time GMing in years (and my very first time in the CoD system), and the format I have makes things go at a smooth and steady clip. I also decided to focus less on the authenticity of the historical city and more on the sort of TV version of 80s Miami. The doc Cocaine Cowboys was incredibly useful, and I'm picking up Miami Babylon from the library this week.<br /> <br /> It was truncated because only three of my (five) players were able to make it, so they didn't make it through the first episode. We'll be introducing the last two characters and finishing off that ep next Sunday. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll fill you guys in on the details then.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for the advice! It was very helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 09-26-2016, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}